---
description: PayFound project architecture, payment safety, and local-first product rules
alwaysApply: true
---
- PayFound is local-store-first. Online/Channel3 offers never prove branch-level stock.
- Retain Metronic React components and AG Grid/AG Studio for tables and dashboards. Do not substitute generic tables when AG Grid serves the purpose.
- All merchant payment actions require PayPal provider confirmation, server-side amounts, stable idempotency keys, and financial reconciliation.
- No autonomous LLM payment, refund, merchant payout, or role escalation. Always require explicit user consent and merchant payment capability.
- Do not call PayPal with production credentials in this prototype; sandbox only. Never store CLIENT_SECRET in React.
- No global stock reservation unless the merchant POS enforces it. Demo atomic holds are valid only for PayFound-owned synthetic stock.
- Separate consumer, merchant, and admin routes at both UI and API layers. Real roles come from server-signed Supabase claims, not client UI selections.
- Use Supabase Postgres/Auth for staging and production; SQLite demo only. Apply migrations, do not depend indefinitely on Base.metadata.create_all.
- DEMO_MODE=true MUST stay localhost-only and be disabled on all public deployments.
- Prefer additive backward-compatible API changes and include tests for success/fail/retry/duplicate events.
- Update docs/STATUS.md and docs/TESTING.md when behaviour or verification changes.
- Keep Kafka/Kubernetes in infra/production until measured need; do not burden hackathon prototype.
- Respect Metronic, AG Studio, PayPal and other sponsor licensing/approvals.
